From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BaresipKit <baresipkit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rtprecv: call the RTP established handler without the
 receiver lock

In the default receive mode rtprecv_decode() called the RTP established
handler while it held the receiver's mutex. The handler raises
CALL_EVENT_RTPESTAB and with it the application's event handlers, which
may call back into baresip. call_answer(), call_progress() and
call_modify() (and so call_hold() and the media direction setters) run
call_update_media(), which reaches rtprecv_enable() through
stream_update() and audio_update(), and rtprecv_enable() takes the same
mutex. The mutex is not recursive, so such a call from the handler
waits for itself and the main thread hangs: an application that answers
an incoming call when its early media arrives never sends the 200.

Note under the mutex that the receiver has just been established and
call the handler after the mutex is released. The rest of the function
already runs without the mutex, and the handler still runs before the
packet is decoded. The handler may have disabled the receiver, so check
that again before the packet goes on to the jitter buffer or decoder.
With the RX thread the handler was already deferred to the main thread
and nothing changes.
---
 src/rtprecv.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/rtprecv.c b/src/rtprecv.c
index b261782..1ca3c18 100644
--- a/src/rtprecv.c
+++ b/src/rtprecv.c
@@ -434,6 +434,7 @@ void rtprecv_decode(const struct sa *src, const struct rtp_header *hdr,
 	struct rtp_receiver *rx = arg;
 	uint32_t ssrc0;
 	bool ssrc_changed = false;
+	bool estab = false;
 	int err = 0;
 
 	if (!rx)
@@ -462,7 +463,7 @@ void rtprecv_decode(const struct sa *src, const struct rtp_header *hdr,
 		if (rx->rtpestabh) {
 			debug("rtprecv: incoming rtp for '%s' established, "
 			      "receiving from %J\n", rx->name, src);
-			pass_rtpestab_work(rx);
+			estab = true;
 		}
 
 		tmr_start(&rx->tmr_decode, 0, decode_tmr, rx);
@@ -486,6 +487,18 @@ void rtprecv_decode(const struct sa *src, const struct rtp_header *hdr,
 	}
 	mtx_unlock(rx->mtx);
 
+	if (estab) {
+		bool enabled;
+
+		pass_rtpestab_work(rx);
+
+		mtx_lock(rx->mtx);
+		enabled = rx->enabled;
+		mtx_unlock(rx->mtx);
+		if (!enabled)
+			return;
+	}
+
 	rtprecv_strip_padding(hdr, mb);
 
 	if (ssrc_changed)
-- 
